+### Detour: `tofu/` OpenTofu provisioning module ([GitHub issue #72](https://github.com/brawer/kube-shim/issues/72)) — ✅ Complete
+
+Not part of the numbered phase sequence -- done out of order, at the user's explicit request, ahead of Phase 17's real-workload testing: before running a real multi-hour job, the user wanted to re-provision their actual production instance properly via OpenTofu (issue #72's own motivation) rather than keep extending the already-compromised, hand-bootstrapped instance, re-keying everything in the process.
+
+**What was built:** a reusable OpenTofu module at `tofu/` -- `upcloud_server` (the host), `upcloud_firewall_rules` (22/443/80 inbound, explicit deny-all else), `tls_private_key` (the shim's own worker-VM SSH keypair, OpenTofu-managed instead of generated by hand), and `random_password` (bearer token(s), `api_token_count`-many, alphanumeric-only -- `random_password`'s own default charset includes `"`/`\`, which would silently corrupt the TOML this module renders them into). First-boot provisioning is fully automated via `user_data` (cloud-init): every step is lifted directly from `bootstrap/provision.sh`'s own already-hands-on-verified sequence, plus one new step that script leaves to a human (non-interactively starting `kube-shim.service` via `machinectl shell` right after `loginctl enable-linger`, retried against a first-boot timing race).
+
+**Two real findings, both caught by actually rendering the templates and checking the output -- not by inspection alone:**
+- `templates/cloud-init.sh.tftpl`'s own bash variables (`$SERVICE_USER`, `$SERVICE_UID`, etc.) collided with `templatefile()`'s identical `${...}` interpolation syntax -- every `${VAR}`-braced bash reference was silently swallowed as an undeclared Terraform variable, caught immediately by `tofu validate` (not something that would have waited for a real apply to surface). Fixed by dropping the braces (`$SERVICE_USER`, safe in every context they're used -- none immediately precede an identifier character) rather than escaping each one with `$$`.
+- `tls_private_key`'s `public_key_openssh` output carries a trailing newline, which lands inside a single-line TOML basic string (`worker_ssh_public_keys = ["..."]`) -- a literal embedded newline there is invalid TOML, not just untidy, and `config.toml` would fail to parse at startup. Caught by actually rendering the template with real (if synthetic) values and feeding the result through this project's own real `Config::from_file` parser, not by eyeballing the output. Fixed with `trimspace()`.
+
+**Deliberately out of scope, documented rather than silently assumed:**
+- DNS record creation (provider-specific; left to the calling root config -- this module only outputs `public_ipv4`).
+- Minting a UpCloud API sub-account token scoped down from full account access for the shim's own runtime use (`var.upcloud_runtime_token`) -- UpCloud's OpenTofu provider has no resource for this at all, confirmed against its real resource list before assuming otherwise.
+- Whether a `tofu apply` that only changes `user_data` (e.g. a credential rotation) takes effect without an explicit reboot, or needs one -- UpCloud's own provider docs don't say, and this hasn't been checked against a real apply yet; `tofu/README.md`'s own "Rotating credentials" section flags this explicitly rather than asserting an unverified behavior.
+
+**Verified:** `tofu validate`/`tofu fmt -check` clean; both templates rendered end-to-end with synthetic values via a scratch root config (never touching any real UpCloud account/token) and the resulting `config.toml` parsed successfully through this project's own real `Config::from_file`; the rendered cloud-init script passed `bash -n`; the base64-embedded quadlet unit content was diffed byte-for-byte against the real, checked-in `deploy/kube-shim.container` and confirmed identical. **Not verified:** a real `tofu apply` against a live UpCloud account -- `tofu/README.md`'s own "Verified vs. not" section says so explicitly, and names the one step (the `machinectl shell` start) most likely to need a fix once that happens.
+
+**Files created:** `tofu/versions.tf`, `tofu/variables.tf`, `tofu/main.tf`, `tofu/outputs.tf`, `tofu/README.md`, `tofu/templates/cloud-init.sh.tftpl`, `tofu/templates/config.toml.tftpl`, `tofu/.terraform.lock.hcl`; `.gitignore` extended for OpenTofu state/provider-cache/tfvars.
+
